\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"84233611bbaa995ae01d6ec401fecf1c303b26b026ed70f7a9a7930b9e37eadf","event_uuid":"a5933804-3e71-4602-a489-6954f0a62077","position":{"commit_sha":"641d128a5c50afdf182b724defad0d642c0a7482","position":"1787161696564901001-a5933804-3e71-4602-a489-6954f0a62077"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f22d55eca6725389ed52165a16f90fe387cb5f1a36f872dc1c594085786d05cb","event_uuid":"0995f155-cd05-416e-a5f7-edff54cfb169","position":{"commit_sha":"06674a4d70d4a32d4190ec3e2b19b3776af1521a","position":"1787162572535343001-0995f155-cd05-416e-a5f7-edff54cfb169"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"c6bd6e4aea975c5a9e7765d733f05aa75c278c37b82ab9fe56329295674ad36e","event_uuid":"5c41f031-3648-454e-84b0-da8e717489c3","position":{"commit_sha":"f1724216e6b2532ef276b46dc8baa146dc9adfa6","position":"1787162617681714001-5c41f031-3648-454e-84b0-da8e717489c3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-232_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"03a4b6e2-5666-42d5-8aaa-0906798afc8f","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"IMPLEMENTED and PUSHED as Gerrit 1906, Change-Id Iadc2675a. Rebased onto origin/main d4acf9c373 first. apply_handlers.py 543 -> 544 (net +1); ADR 0099 294 -> 458 lines.\n\nTHE CUT: three lines became one. `entry = ctx.binding_store.all_bindings().get(local_id)` plus the isinstance guard plus `peer_state.note_rich_emit(entry, wire)` became `ctx.binding_store.note_rich_emit(local_id, wire) != peer_state.RICH_REEMIT_OBSERVE_AT`. The missing binding stays nonfatal because the operation returns None, deliberately distinct from 0, so one equality covers both the absent binding and the below-threshold case. Diff stayed tight to _observe_rich_reemit and its docstring; _rich_cutover_active untouched as required.\n\nFIFTH FALSE DOCUMENTED CLAIM OF THIS EPIC, and the one that had been actively load-bearing: the docstring justified mutation-through-query with \"binding_store.py sits at the module-size cap and cannot carry a narrower accessor\". Both halves were false - S2 T3 added the accessor, and that file is 554 lines. The pattern across all five is consistent: a workaround outlives the constraint that justified it, and the comment explaining the workaround is what keeps it alive. A test now asserts the phrase is gone, and it is mutation-verified.\n\nTHE CENSUS IS AN ALLOWLIST, NOT A BAN, AND IT IS PARSED RATHER THAN GREPPED. The reviewer's plan-review advisory asked how the census would distinguish a MUTATION through all_bindings() from a benign READ, which was the right question: four production readers legitimately iterate through it (binding_walk, reconcile_helpers, reconcile_check, _commands/bridge_repair), and I verified each by reading the call site - every write in those modules goes through a named facade method (set_baseline, merge_baseline, unbind). So the test records which callers may call it and why, and a NEW caller fails until someone classifies it in writing. It uses ast to find real Call nodes: a substring search matched four extra files that only DISCUSS all_bindings() in prose, and those are the files most likely to mention it and least likely to misuse it.\n\nADR 0099 FINALIZED. It described a plan; it now records what landed, and states which parts are behaviour rather than intention so weakening one is a behaviour change, not a plan revision. Realized classifier rules, tombstone authority versus explicit unretire, the intentional behaviour delta and its rollback, and the no-broad-staging prohibition are all in. The section that matters most records the invocation boundary AND why run_differs.py cannot host it, then instructs whoever next splits the capped reconcile.py to keep the call between the staleness gate and the first fetch, naming test_repair_runs_before_the_first_remote_observation as the oracle. RP-03 S5 is queued against that file, so the instruction has a known audience - also filed as insectile-modest-martin (d7b9-ac42-ad6f-4608).\n\nTWO ADR CLAIMS HAD GONE STALE UNDER RP-04 AND ARE CORRECTED. Section 9 said cutting the lifecycle config reads to a seam was \"still not RP-02's work\" and that both legacy-exception rows had been re-registered under binding_lifecycle.py. RP-04 C3g (toadyish-magic-arrowana) has since made that cut: _env_int is gone from all of src/, binding_lifecycle.py no longer references os, note_absent calls resolve_absent_retire_grace(), and the exceptions registry is drained to EMPTY so those rows no longer exist. Behaviour preserved - same variable, default 3, clamp to minimum 1. The companion claim that docs/env-vars.md records line numbers for those reads is void now the reads are gone; the general lesson is kept in one sentence because it bit three times in this epic. The implementer verified every one of these independently rather than trusting my summary.\n\nA HAZARD I CHECKED AND CLEARED rather than assumed: the set_flag fixture in the rich-reemit suite patches rebar.config.load_config, while RP-04 changed _rich_cutover_active to call compose_config(). I suspected the fixture had gone inert - which would have made the production oracles vacuous exactly where I needed them as the regression half - and probed it. compose_config() delegates to load_config internally, so the fixture is live and the oracles are meaningful. Worth recording because the real project config has rich_text_cutover = 'cloud', so the flag is ON by default and an inert fixture would NOT have shown up as a failure.\n\nHELD-OUT TDD: 36 oracles, of which the 29 pre-existing tests are the compatibility half and had to pass UNCHANGED - the cutover is required to be behaviour-preserving, so a change in the counter progression, the single read-back, the baseline route or the fail-open branches would be a regression rather than an improvement. The implementer saw 34; 2 discriminators were held outside the worktree and both passed unseen. Implementer: 1 attempt per part, and it verified it had touched no test file by hash.\n\nMUTATION: 3 of 4 killed - reverting to mutation-through-query, turning the equality threshold into a floor, and restoring the false accessor claim. The fourth SURVIVED and is a provably EQUIVALENT mutant, not an oracle gap: coercing the missing binding's None to 0 cannot be observed because RICH_REEMIT_OBSERVE_AT is 2, so a coerced 0 never equals it. I did NOT manufacture a test for it, applying the same judgement S2 T2 used for the unobservable env clamp - such a test could only assert implementation. It does surface a mild overstatement: the facade docstring says a 0 \"would trigger the caller's read-back for a binding that is not there\", which holds only if the threshold were ever lowered to 0 or 1. The None remains the right defensive choice; the hazard is latent, not present. Recorded rather than chased, since correcting it means editing binding_store.py, which is outside this task's declared impact.\n\nGATES: 3455 passed / 9 skipped across the reconciler unit tree, interfaces/store, reconciler integration, the docs-index and ADR-number suites and the comment-hygiene guard; lint clean, mypy 567, complexity new=0 increased=0, comment hygiene, config ownership, env registry unchanged.","timestamp":1787156976713593001}],"created_at":1787027744891207001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"5f4dd1cd-c7b3-468c-a968-ff2eb37ab124","relation":"depends_on","target_id":"90a5-6a33-5cda-4064"},{"link_uuid":"19b6405e-2272-4df3-beca-5b31aae63e33","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1700-7e4c-cc8f-4f2c"},{"link_uuid":"b58edab4-9946-4783-bfd7-11ad88b83ff9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d916-3882-4d35-4b03"},{"link_uuid":"278b03bd-314f-4ff3-989b-863a87a8f501","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"197d-409f-f807-4384"}],"description":"## Context\nThe narrow rich-emission operation `BindingStore.note_rich_emit` exists after S2, but production still mutates a binding reached through `all_bindings()` in `apply_handlers._observe_rich_reemit`. That call site's docstring also justifies the mutation-through-query with a claim that is now FALSE: it says `binding_store.py` \"sits at the module-size cap and cannot carry a narrower accessor\". S2 T3 added exactly such an accessor, and `binding_store.py` is no longer at the cap. ADR 0099 also needs the realized recovery boundary and reversal rules.\n\n## Outcome\nRoute production rich-emission state through the authoritative facade, remove production mutation-through-query, correct the false accessor claim at that call site, and finalize ADR 0099 without changing output, storage, or tickets publication.\n\n## Plan\n1. RP-04 S3 `talismanic-profitable-isopod` is closed, so its landed `apply_handlers.py` is the implementation base. Rebase before starting; RP-04 S7.3.a `insincere-illogical-antlion` is in progress on the same file.\n2. Replace only the rich-emission inner-dict mutation with `BindingStore.note_rich_emit(local_id, wire)`, which returns the emission count or `None` for a missing binding and performs NO save of its own. Preserve hashes, counters, missing-binding fail-open behavior, logs, and baseline effects exactly.\n3. Correct the docstring's accessor claim in the same change. Keep the diff tight to `_observe_rich_reemit` and its docstring; do NOT reflow the adjacent `_rich_cutover_active`.\n4. Add a production census test that fails if any production module reaches a binding mutation through `all_bindings()`.\n5. Finalize ADR 0099 with tombstone authority, explicit-unretire reversal, the realized pre-observation repair boundary, intentional delta, rollback, and the ban on broad tickets-branch staging.\n\n## Testing\nRun rich-reemit, apply-handler, recovery-boundary, and ADR index suites against the RP-04-integrated base.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Production rich-emission behavior uses the narrow facade operation.\n- [x] Existing hashes, counters, logs, and missing-binding outcomes are preserved.\n- [x] No production code mutates a binding through `all_bindings()`.\n- [x] The rich-emission call site carries no false claim that `binding_store.py` cannot carry a narrower accessor.\n- [x] Binding and event file bytes and selective publication are unchanged outside the approved repair.\n- [x] ADR 0099 records the realized repair rule and its rollback.\n- [x] ADR 0099 names the pre-observation boundary AND the actual invocation site in `reconcile.py` after the under-lock staleness gate, and why the invocation is not in `run_differs.py`.\n- [x] ADR 0099 records explicit-unretire reversal and the prohibition on broad tickets-branch staging.\n\n## Out of scope\nConfiguration and secrets changes remain owned by RP-04.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_handlers.py","reason":"Cut production rich-emission mutation to the narrow facade operation and correct the now-false accessor claim."},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"Correct the all_bindings docstring, which this cut makes false where it names the rich-text handler as a mutator."},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py","reason":"Production cutover compatibility, narrow-operation, and mutation-through-query census tests."},{"path":"docs/adr/0099-binding-store-internal-ownership.md","reason":"Finalize repair, invocation boundary, reversal, rollback, and staging decisions."},{"path":"docs/adr/README.md","reason":"Keep ADR index current."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["depends_on","90a5-6a33-5cda-4064"],["parent","486a-69ef-6370-48ff"],["relates_to","1700-7e4c-cc8f-4f2c"],["relates_to","197d-409f-f807-4384"],["relates_to","d916-3882-4d35-4b03"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"486a-69ef-6370-48ff","parent_status_uuid":"0995f155-cd05-416e-a5f7-edff54cfb169","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["rp02","binding-recovery","adr","tdd"],"ticket_id":"ef69-e27b-d02d-4eef","ticket_type":"task","title":"RP-02 S3 T3 — Cut rich-emission writes to the facade and finalize ADR 0099","verify_commands":[{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_rich_reemit_state.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/apply/test_apply_handlers_neutral_assignee.py tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/orchestrate/test_recovery_write_boundary.py","dd_id":"AC1-AC4","dd_text":"RP-04 base guard, production facade cutover, mutation census, and byte/publication compatibility"},{"command":"env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/pytest -q tests/unit/test_check_docs_index.py tests/scripts/test_check_adr_numbers.py","dd_id":"AC5","dd_text":"ADR numbering and documentation index"}]},"source_event_uuids":["5187ecc1-4531-41db-a1b8-bae44cc07e3d","b083f40a-d078-4c93-8fd0-8c5e93d1cffd","82d519ca-ddc7-4ea1-bae4-6684f0c4f190","43f5d508-3d03-4f15-b272-779748760288","c3462879-5dab-4018-9b88-9195904fb0ce","19b6405e-2272-4df3-beca-5b31aae63e33","36a43da0-9c34-49aa-9a08-1663bc76d7bb","35fde2ad-00d3-42da-9918-cef4a83f1247","b58edab4-9946-4783-bfd7-11ad88b83ff9","278b03bd-314f-4ff3-989b-863a87a8f501","09551a70-5d62-4990-8a5d-ea3cf6081f8e","a5933804-3e71-4602-a489-6954f0a62077","0995f155-cd05-416e-a5f7-edff54cfb169","5c41f031-3648-454e-84b0-da8e717489c3"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787169232528237001,"uuid":"8eadb0e3-a4e5-47aa-97e5-d151cce3ab27"}